# Task 5 report — atomic schema-v4 optimizer roles

Date: 2026-08-31

## Scope completed

- Added an additive schema-v4 optimizer manifest and canonical v4 loader while
  retaining schema-v3 dataclasses, prompts, response schemas, parser, and call
  budgets unchanged for legacy audit loading.
- Bound v4 campaign/sequence, clean source identity, policy interface 2, PIT
  bundle, exact discovery-plan digest, qualification-plan commitment,
  `AnnualizedReturnTarget`, optional seed-checkpoint digest, ordered editable
  paths, immutable constraints, digest-pinned sandbox, a complete `3 * N` role
  call plan, `apply=false`, and zero provider retries. Run lengths greater than
  two iterations are accepted.
- Added `PolicyAuthoringScopeV4` with hashes for exactly three initial policy
  sources, an actual escaped canonical source-envelope byte count, finite
  feedback/history/headroom and per-call response/token bounds, and descendant
  rule `authenticated_parent_plus_atomic_full_sources`. No patch, hunk, changed
  line, diff-byte, file-choice, 64-KiB change, or USD limit is present in v4.
- Added self-authenticating baseline/champion/branch
  `SelectedParentIdentity`, aggregate-only `SelectedParentSummary`, and bound
  investigator/author/critic inputs. Source bundles are checked against the
  selected parent's ordered per-file digests and canonical bundle digest.
- Added strict investigator and critic v4 outputs. Investigator focus areas are
  one to three values from `entry`, `risk_sizing`, and `exit` in canonical
  order. Critic disposition is exactly `promote`, `refine`, or `abandon`, with
  no v3 alias normalization.
- Added the atomic `AuthorArtifactV4` response: exactly the three complete
  editable sources, strict recursive duplicate-key rejection, strict UTF-8
  including surrogate rejection, LF-only/no-NUL/no-CR/final-LF source rules,
  canonical internal path order, parent binding, and at least one source change
  versus the authenticated parent. It exposes no candidate workspace or patch.
- Added panel/CAGR feedback contracts, compact prior hypotheses, validation
  status, content-free `AuthorManifestSummaryV4`, author-only
  `RoleOutputInvalidSummary`, and the valid-author-manifest XOR invalid-author
  branch in `CriticInputV4`. Critic inputs contain no policy source text.
- Added versioned v4 prompts, strict local response parsers, closed response
  schemas, and prompt/schema/source-aware byte validation.
- Exposed closed primitive decoders for the Task-4 annualized target and
  `PanelAggregateSummary`; aggregate decoding requires exact keys and nested
  metrics and reuses the Task-4 production CAGR/0.01 validation.
- Updated only existing test functions/helpers and assertions; no test file,
  test function, or test class was added. Legacy loop/controller wiring was
  intentionally not changed because candidate writes, authorization, control
  flow, accounting, checkpointing, and qualification belong to Tasks 6–9.

