## Self-review against Task 5

1. Schema-v4 is additive; v3 remains separately parseable for audit and its
   production definitions were not retrofitted.
2. V4 authoring scope measures the escaped source envelope and has no patch or
   financial ceiling.
3. Parent identities self-authenticate; role and author-result bindings check
   parent/source digests; baseline is explicit and non-null.
4. Author parsing is closed and atomic across exactly three complete sources,
   validates all text before return, and rejects a no-op bundle.
5. V4 feedback is panel/CAGR-only, validates quick/discovery IDs and Decimal
   CAGR, and the invalid-author critic alternative is content-free and XOR.
6. V4 prompts/schemas are versioned, strict, and locally revalidated; v4 critic
   literals have no aliases while v3 behavior remains untouched.
7. No controller, candidate workspace, authorization/accounting, checkpoint,
   rollback, or qualification behavior was added.

