## Review fix round 1

### Scope and files

The review fixes remain additive schema-v4 contract work. They modify only
`core/pit_optimization_contract.py` and existing assertions/helpers in
`tests/test_pit_optimizer_v2.py`; no new test file, test function, or test class
was added. `core/pit_optimizer_evaluation.py` did not need a production change
because the Task-4 panel and target primitives already supply the required
identity and precision contracts. No Task 6–9 controller, candidate-write,
authorization, checkpoint, rollback, or qualification behavior was wired.

### Review findings resolved

- Added the Task-4 quick- and discovery-panel digests to the v4 manifest and
  every role context, deriving them directly from `DiscoveryPanelPlan` and
  authenticating them against the supplied manifest during call-budget
  validation. Investigator selected/baseline/champion/branch summaries and
  critic selected/candidate/baseline/champion summaries now require the exact
  expected panel digest and purpose. `TargetProgressV4` is recomputed from the
  exact discovery summaries and compared field-for-field, including all CAGR
  scalars and the target gap. Parent selection is deterministic: an active
  branch wins, otherwise the champion wins, otherwise the baseline wins.
- Made the v4 feedback/history declarations operational. Scope construction
  rejects investigator source+feedback+history, author source+feedback, or
  critic feedback declarations that exceed the corresponding dynamic call
  cap. Each role budget check now requires the exact manifest, scope digest,
  ordered call-budget slot, and canonical serialized feedback/history
  envelopes, while retaining the full canonical input-payload cap. These are
  finite byte/call/token caps only; no patch, diff, changed-line, USD, or old
  64-KiB policy-change ceiling was introduced.
- Extended the content-free `RoleOutputInvalidSummary` with its positive
  iteration and deterministic author `call_index`. Critic construction binds
  both values to the current iteration's author slot. The invalid-author branch
  requires `invalid/author_output_invalid` and cannot carry candidate evidence;
  every `valid` status requires both quick and discovery panels, while invalid
  and not-evaluated statuses reject both.
- Restored DeepSeek/OpenRouter compatibility by making
  `pit_optimizer_v4_response_format()` return generic JSON-object mode. The
  versioned closed role schemas remain available through
  `pit_optimizer_v4_response_schema()` for local introspection. Authoritative
  local dataclass constructors and parsers now enforce the schema limits,
  including 256-character narrative/behavior fields and 96-character compact
  list items; 257- and 97-character values are rejected.

