### Self-review and concerns

- Schema-v3 dataclasses/loaders/prompts/budgets remain untouched and v3 remains
  audit-only; all new binding and transport behavior is v4-only.
- Qualification data is not present in any role input. Only the already
  authorized discovery-plan digest remains in role context, while the manifest
  retains the qualification commitment required by Task 4.
- Panel identities use the Task-4 `EvaluationPanelSpec.sha256` dialect; source
  bundles retain their distinct newline-committed canonical digest dialect.
- Call validation authenticates both declared component envelopes and the full
  canonical role payload, so envelope accounting does not replace the actual
  transport cap.
- Remaining red tests are outside Task 5 ownership and were intentionally not
  chased. No provider call, Docker/replay run, secret inspection, push,
  progress-ledger edit, or original-checkout mutation occurred.
